Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:53:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-70: one Enter for Alias; a BCB6 handler -> the
 port's C++ through a named command (0.70.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "我更改alias後按下enter需要操作兩次才輸入得進去", and on main.html's Exit
button: "BCB 就可以對應到 void __fastcall TfMain::sbCloseProgramClick，你這邊怎不行對應到?"
- Alias / Name: the panel was drawn again from the SOURCE text before the edit
  reached it -- the field showed the old Alias, so a second Enter. Alias is now
  read from the page (the probe changes the title before it asks again). And
  the field commits on Enter's key release too (the IO names' suggestion list
  can take the key press) and on a name picked from the list, never twice.
- the command trace resolves a command held in a name: raw(CMD, ...) with
  var CMD = 'act.main.closeProgram' (ht9045_main_close.js:40). So the Exit
  button's OnClick = BCB6 sbCloseProgramClick AND the port's
  W906_Main_CloseProgramOp (FileRW/MainClose.cpp:1318) through
  act.main.closeProgram; a .dfm event gets the 網頁 / 伺服器 marks and the
  port's function too (its handler name stays the .dfm's).
- vscode_it.ps1: a page put back to exactly its committed text while the test
  ran (another session reverted HW.IoSetView.html mid-run at 14:39:14, same
  MD5 as HEAD) is theirs when the test saved nothing -- a WARN, not a FAIL.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 154, smoke 156, real VS Code 143): lib (raw(CMD)
resolved), panels (one Enter + key release + change + blur = ONE setAlias),
real VS Code (BtnPanelLane3's Alias changed once -> the panel shows the new
one, reverted; main.html sbCloseProgram OnClick -> act.main.closeProgram ->
W906_Main_CloseProgramOp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
